# The old public hostname after the cutover (#52). Paste this site block into the Caddyfile of
# the Caddy that serves the old host, replace the two host names, copy sw.js (next to this
# file) to /srv/bookclub-legacy-origin/sw.js on that machine, then `caddy reload`.
#
# Every path redirects permanently (301) to the same path and query on the new host. /sw.js is
# the exception: a browser does not follow a redirect when it checks its service worker for
# updates, so the old offline worker of installed apps would stay. /sw.js serves a worker that
# deletes the old caches and unregisters itself (docs/phase1/spec/platform.md, risk R22).
#
# `redir` sits inside `handle`: Caddy orders the redir directive before handle, so a bare redir
# at the top of the block would also redirect /sw.js.
#
# Check it before the reload:
#   caddy validate --config Caddyfile --adapter caddyfile
# and afterwards (docs/phase2/cutover.md):
#   curl -sI https://old.example/shelf?x=1   301, Location: https://new.example/shelf?x=1
#   curl -sI https://old.example/sw.js       200, text/javascript, Cache-Control: no-store
#
# The {$VAR:default} placeholders let `caddy validate` and the local check run as they are;
# for the local check, BOOKCLUB_OLD_HOST=http://:8085 serves the block over plain HTTP.

{$BOOKCLUB_OLD_HOST:old.example} {
	handle /sw.js {
		root * /srv/bookclub-legacy-origin
		header Content-Type "text/javascript; charset=utf-8"
		header Cache-Control "no-store"
		file_server
	}
	handle {
		redir https://{$BOOKCLUB_NEW_HOST:new.example}{uri} permanent
	}
}
